title: VMware vCenter Server Appliance: Proxy Configuration
agents: vcsa_health
catalog: app/vmware
license: GPL-2.0-only
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check reports the HTTP, HTTPS and FTP proxy configuration of a VMware
 vCenter Server Appliance (VCSA). The data is retrieved by the special agent
 {agent_vcsa_health}.

 A broken or changed proxy stops the appliance reaching the update
 repository, so the configuration is worth watching where one is in use. The
 service is {OK} by default; the ruleset "VCSA proxy configuration" allows a
 site to declare that no proxy should be enabled.

discovery:
 One service is created only on appliances where at least one proxy protocol
 is enabled. Appliances without a proxy get no service.
